WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.035
-On our last show before break,
we did a bit with Addison Rae

00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:06.005
where she taught me
eight viral TikTok dances.

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:08.174
Now, we recognize that
the creators of those dances

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:10.043
deserve to have
their own spotlight.

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.144
So right now some of
the creators will join me

00:00:12.144 --> 00:00:14.480
to talk about
how their dance went viral

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.916
and then perform
the dance themselves.

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.151
Up first, we've got

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:20.986
Mya Nicole Johnson
and Chris Cotter,

00:00:20.986 --> 00:00:23.689
who created the viral dance
to Cardi B's "Up."

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:24.991
Hey, Mya. Hey, Chris.

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:26.525
-Hi.
-Hello.

00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:28.193
-Thanks for coming on
"The Tonight Show"

00:00:28.193 --> 00:00:29.729
all the way from Houston.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:32.465
-Thank you for having us.
-Please.

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:34.633
How long have you guys
known each other?

00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:36.936
-It's been about --
It's gonna be two years.

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:41.640
-What is it like to choreograph
these dances together as a team?

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.510
-It's really fun, especially
when we're both really creative.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:46.746
So when we put our dances
together,

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:49.081
it just makes it even better.

00:00:49.081 --> 00:00:51.785
-And you came up with the dance
to "Up" by Cardi B.

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:53.319
What made you go with "Up"?

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:55.354
-So, basically, we already knew

00:00:55.354 --> 00:00:57.956
that we were linking up
prior to the video.

00:00:57.956 --> 00:01:00.125
And so we already knew
that Cardi B had just came out

00:01:00.125 --> 00:01:02.128
with a new song called "Up"
and it was going viral.

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:04.730
Everyone was, like,
listening to the song.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:06.966
So we knew that if we were to
make, like, a challenge to it,

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:09.302
it had potential of going viral.

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:11.904
-Now, Cardi B herself
even reposted it.

00:01:11.904 --> 00:01:14.673
How great was that
when you saw what she did?

00:01:14.673 --> 00:01:15.942
-That was really exciting.

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:18.545
She posted our video two times
on her Instagram

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:19.845
and then one time on TikTok.

00:01:19.845 --> 00:01:22.048
So yeah, that was
a great experience.

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:23.416
-I love it. Alright.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:26.352
You're gonna perform your "Up"
dance for us right now.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.087
Whenever you guys are ready,
take it away.

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:29.188
Thank you for being here.

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:37.463 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:45.771 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:45.771 --> 00:01:47.573
[ Cheers and applause ]
See, that's how you do it.

00:01:47.573 --> 00:01:48.875
That's what I'm talking about.

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:52.645
Mya Nicole Johnson
and Chris Cotter.

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:59.252 line:0%
Check them out on TikTok
@theemyanicole and @cchrvs.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.654
Thank you guys so much
for coming on.

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:03.156
-Thank you so much.

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:06.492
-Next, we have the creator
of the Corvette Corvette dance,

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:09.595
Dorian Scott,
a.k.a. Yvnggprince Dorian.

00:02:09.595 --> 00:02:11.197
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Hi. How are you?

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:12.264
-I'm doing good, buddy.

00:02:12.264 --> 00:02:13.566
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:14.801
I appreciate it.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.068
Tell us a little bit
about yourself.

00:02:16.068 --> 00:02:18.671
I know -- Are you from Philly?

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:20.807
-Yes. I'm from
North Philadelphia.

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:22.441
Actually born and raised,
and my mom

00:02:22.441 --> 00:02:24.177
is always telling me
to put school first,

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:26.879
so I want to let y'all know
that I'm a freshman

00:02:26.879 --> 00:02:29.816
at the University of Delaware,
studying visual communications.

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:32.752
But I also a model
and can dance.

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:33.819
-There you go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:35.054
School first.

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:37.089
I agree. Your mom's right.

00:02:37.089 --> 00:02:39.492
You created
the Corvette Corvette dance,

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:42.161
which is to the song
"Adderall (Corvette Corvette)"

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:43.696
by Popp Hunna.

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:46.565
Now, have you been dancing
for a long time?

00:02:46.565 --> 00:02:47.901
-Yes, honestly,
I've been dancing

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.068
since before I can remember.

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:51.370
But I started off as a gymnast.

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:55.574
I finished third in a region
from New York to Virginia.

00:02:55.574 --> 00:02:57.477
And then I started
focusing more on my dance.

00:02:57.477 --> 00:02:59.845
And fast-forward to TikTok,

00:02:59.845 --> 00:03:01.480
I'm making a lot
of dance videos on there.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:04.650
And I used to get like
500,000 views, a million.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:06.519
So the artists
actually hit me up

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:08.487
and asked me
to dance to their song

00:03:08.487 --> 00:03:09.822
and make it a challenge.

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.891
-Now, where do you go from here?

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:15.027
What do you hope to be doing
in the next few years?

00:03:15.027 --> 00:03:18.964
-So I want to be an all-around
performer, entertainer.

00:03:18.964 --> 00:03:20.967
Will Smith and Kevin Hart,
they're like my inspirations.

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:25.037
I love their journey, and one of
my dream roles would be to play

00:03:25.037 --> 00:03:28.040
a live-action version
of Miles Morales as Spider-Man.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.009
-Spider-Man?
-Yeah.

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.177
I told you I was a gymnast,

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.578
so you know
I got the moves and stuff.

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:34.547
And I think I think I look
kind of good in tights.

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:37.049
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:39.519
-Alright, there's your next
Spider-Man right there.

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:40.687
Now you're going to perform

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:43.790
the Corvette Corvette dance
for all of us.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.024
Please, whenever you're ready,
buddy,

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:46.492
and thank you again, Dorian.

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:54.367 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:54.367 --> 00:04:02.275 line:0%
♪♪

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:03.843
Yo, come on!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:05.811
That's how you do it
right there!

00:04:05.811 --> 00:04:08.815
You can see more
from Dorian on TikTok.

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:13.052 line:0%
His handle is @yvnggprince.

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:15.255 line:0%
Thank you so much
for being here, bud.

00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:16.856
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:19.825
-Up next, he created
the Laffy Taffy Remix

00:04:19.825 --> 00:04:22.161
and she came up with the dance.

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:25.164
Here are Fly Boy Fu and Indii.

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:26.198
[ Cheers and applause ]
Hi!

00:04:26.198 --> 00:04:28.433
-Hello. How are you?
-Look at you.

00:04:28.433 --> 00:04:30.002
Good to see you guys.

00:04:30.002 --> 00:04:32.971
Fu, you made this remix
about 10 years ago,

00:04:32.971 --> 00:04:35.608
and now it became
huge on TikTok.

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:38.711
How did you find out that
it had gotten so popular?

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:41.581
-I was on social media
a while back, like,

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:43.148
before my parents
had passed away.

00:04:43.148 --> 00:04:46.419
And I heard A-DuB, the producer
here, put this beat out.

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:48.954
And he was like, "I need lyrics
for this, this beat."

00:04:48.954 --> 00:04:50.823
And I liked the beat.
It was really, really catchy.

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:52.591
So I went in the studio,

00:04:52.591 --> 00:04:54.994
in my parents' studio,
and then I just closed my eyes

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:56.329
and I started to freestyle.

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:57.997
And that was the first take.

00:04:57.997 --> 00:04:59.798
I just sent it over to him.
-One take.

00:04:59.798 --> 00:05:03.769
-And he made the track.
-Wow!

00:05:03.769 --> 00:05:06.905
And, Indii, you came up
with the dance.

00:05:06.905 --> 00:05:08.441
Did you know it was
going to go viral

00:05:08.441 --> 00:05:10.709
or you're just hoping
and you're just like,

00:05:10.709 --> 00:05:12.311
"I'm just gonna try this"?

00:05:12.311 --> 00:05:15.014
-I made the dance just because,

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:17.650
and then two years later,
look, it's on TikTok.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:20.686
It's viral. I'm like --
It's shocking, because, like,

00:05:20.686 --> 00:05:22.888
I wasn't even expecting it
to go viral.

00:05:22.888 --> 00:05:26.258
-How long does it take you
to come up with a dance?

00:05:26.258 --> 00:05:27.427
-Like about five minutes.

00:05:27.427 --> 00:05:29.027
I had made it on the bus
because I went to school,

00:05:29.027 --> 00:05:30.095
and then when I got home,

00:05:30.095 --> 00:05:32.198
I recorded the dance
and posted it.

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:34.366
-You say you made it on the bus?

00:05:34.366 --> 00:05:36.569
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:38.371
That's fantastic.

00:05:38.371 --> 00:05:41.340
I want to see the dance
if you don't mine.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.275
Ladies and gentlemen,
here's Indii performing

00:05:43.275 --> 00:05:45.778
"Laffy Taffy Remix" by Fu.

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:46.946
Take it away.

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:55.221 line:0%
♪♪

00:05:55.221 --> 00:06:03.529 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:07.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:10.736
Check out Fly Boy Fu and Indii
on TikTok

00:06:10.736 --> 00:06:15.207 line:0%
@flyboyfu and @17slumz.

00:06:15.207 --> 00:06:16.808 line:0%
Thank you again
for being here, you guys.

00:06:16.808 --> 00:06:19.478
I really appreciate it.
-Thank you for having us.

00:06:19.478 --> 00:06:21.680
-Good luck with whatever
you do next.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:25.017
Next up are the creators
of the Blinding Lights dance,

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:28.054
Greg Dahl, Adam Snyder,
and Nate Nale.

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:30.522
[ Cheers and applause ]
Hello, guys.

00:06:30.522 --> 00:06:32.525
-How are you doing?
-Nice to see you.

00:06:32.525 --> 00:06:38.664
Now, you all share
the TikTok handle @macdaddyz.

00:06:38.664 --> 00:06:41.300
How do you all know each other?

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.035
-So, actually,
first and foremost,

00:06:43.035 --> 00:06:44.837
thanks for having us on.
We really appreciate it.

00:06:44.837 --> 00:06:46.205
But to the question,

00:06:46.205 --> 00:06:48.074
we're actually
roommates for the past two years

00:06:48.074 --> 00:06:51.076
at Immaculata University
in Pennsylvania.

00:06:51.076 --> 00:06:52.978
But that's kind of how
the whole friendship started

00:06:52.978 --> 00:06:55.080
and the account really
was created through that.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:57.650
-Now, how did the Blinding
Lights dance come to be?

00:06:57.650 --> 00:07:00.486
'Cause I heard it started with
the foot move,

00:07:00.486 --> 00:07:02.555
which is basically
about as far as I can go.

00:07:02.555 --> 00:07:04.924
But what is the story
behind the whole deal?

00:07:04.924 --> 00:07:06.993
-Yeah.
So I've actually been like

00:07:06.993 --> 00:07:08.894
a huge fan
of The Weeknd for a while.

00:07:08.894 --> 00:07:12.498
And when that song first came
out, I was listening to it

00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:14.834
all the time,
playing it at school.

00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:16.802
And just one night,
we were dancing to it.

00:07:16.802 --> 00:07:18.804
And the foot move, actually,

00:07:18.804 --> 00:07:21.206
that was like
our go-to dance back then.

00:07:21.206 --> 00:07:24.243
So we put that in there and we
added some hand movements,

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:27.713
and it just kind of went
together perfectly.

00:07:27.713 --> 00:07:29.882
-You're going to perform
the Blinding Lights dance

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:31.583
for us now on
"The Tonight Show."

00:07:31.583 --> 00:07:33.085
Are you guys ready?

00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:36.121
-Oh, we're ready.
-Go for it whenever.

00:07:36.121 --> 00:07:42.761 line:0%
♪♪

00:07:42.761 --> 00:07:49.401 line:0%
♪♪

00:07:49.401 --> 00:07:51.770
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:54.573
There you go.

00:07:54.573 --> 00:07:56.742
-Thank you so much.
-Yeah, thanks for having us.

00:07:56.742 --> 00:07:59.478
-You can follow Greg, Adam,
and Nate on TikTok.

00:07:59.478 --> 00:08:03.316 line:0%
Their handle is @macdaddyz.

00:08:03.316 --> 00:08:05.317 line:0%
Thanks for coming on the show,
guys.

00:08:05.317 --> 00:08:09.421
And finally, please say hello to
the creator of the Savage dance,

00:08:09.421 --> 00:08:13.326
Keara Wilson, a.k.a. Queen Keke!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:13.326 --> 00:08:16.495
-Hello, everyone.
-Hi, Keara.

00:08:16.495 --> 00:08:18.764
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:21.833
-Thank you for having me.
-Now, for over a year,

00:08:21.833 --> 00:08:24.203
everyone on TikTok
has been doing your dance

00:08:24.203 --> 00:08:26.171
to Megan Thee Stallion's song
"Savage."

00:08:26.171 --> 00:08:28.341
Can you take me back to the day
that you created it?

00:08:28.341 --> 00:08:31.377
Like, what led up to
you posting it?

00:08:31.377 --> 00:08:32.745
-Absolutely.

00:08:32.745 --> 00:08:36.415
I just had moved to Texas
from Ohio to be with my sister.

00:08:36.415 --> 00:08:38.818
So, she was about
to have her baby.

00:08:38.818 --> 00:08:41.920
At that time, I just had
graduated high school

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:44.389
and I didn't know what I wanted
to do with my life.

00:08:44.389 --> 00:08:48.394
So basically,
I needed an outlet to destress.

00:08:48.394 --> 00:08:50.629
So I downloaded TikTok.

00:08:50.629 --> 00:08:52.330
I've been dancing for 10 years.

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:54.967
And I seen that people were
doing a bunch of dances

00:08:54.967 --> 00:08:57.837
on TikTok,
so I wanted to try it too.

00:08:57.837 --> 00:09:00.405
So I made one up, you know?

00:09:00.405 --> 00:09:03.009
And it took me about 30 minutes
to choreograph

00:09:03.009 --> 00:09:04.910
because I kept changing
the ending.

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:07.713
Originally the ending
was really hard.

00:09:07.713 --> 00:09:10.249
But I'm actually glad
I didn't change it.

00:09:10.249 --> 00:09:11.917
-I think the whole
thing is hard.

00:09:11.917 --> 00:09:14.553
Can you show me
what was the hard ending?

00:09:14.553 --> 00:09:16.389
Could you show me
what that was like?

00:09:16.389 --> 00:09:17.723
-Yeah.

00:09:17.723 --> 00:09:25.264 line:0%
♪♪

00:09:25.264 --> 00:09:32.804 line:0%
♪♪

00:09:32.804 --> 00:09:36.008
-That's what I'm talking about.
That's my favorite part.

00:09:36.008 --> 00:09:37.776
That is so great.

00:09:37.776 --> 00:09:39.411
What is it like to be able

00:09:39.411 --> 00:09:43.549
to see your dance catch on
and become viral?

00:09:43.549 --> 00:09:46.285
-I never expected to it blow up
like it did.

00:09:46.285 --> 00:09:48.421
I just did it for fun, honestly.

00:09:48.421 --> 00:09:50.822
Then I just kept seeing it grow.

00:09:50.822 --> 00:09:53.993
Celebrities were doing it.
Little kids were doing it.

00:09:53.993 --> 00:09:55.661
It was the best.

00:09:55.661 --> 00:09:59.831
But I would have to say,
seeing my dance bring joy

00:09:59.831 --> 00:10:04.269
to people throughout quarantine
was definitely the best part.

00:10:04.269 --> 00:10:05.571
-Yeah. We love it too,

00:10:05.571 --> 00:10:07.506
and I'm so happy
that you came on the show.

00:10:07.506 --> 00:10:09.408
I also want to say
congratulations are in order.

00:10:09.408 --> 00:10:11.944
You're engaged.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:11.944 --> 00:10:13.579
Yeah! That's what
I'm talking about.

00:10:13.579 --> 00:10:19.718
Now, how much pressure
is on your fiancé now?

00:10:19.718 --> 00:10:24.156
-Oh, my gosh, a lot
because I'm going to

00:10:24.156 --> 00:10:26.859
make up some cool dances,
and he can't really dance.

00:10:26.859 --> 00:10:29.127
[ Laughter ]
He has rhythm.

00:10:29.127 --> 00:10:31.263
-Good luck, buddy!
-He has rhythm.

00:10:31.263 --> 00:10:33.065
[ Laughter ]

00:10:33.065 --> 00:10:34.333
-It's gonna be fun.

00:10:34.333 --> 00:10:35.701
Everyone's gonna look forward
to that.

00:10:35.701 --> 00:10:37.136
Thank you so much
for coming on our show.

00:10:37.136 --> 00:10:38.370
Keara Wilson.

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:43.476 line:0%
Follow her on TikTok
@keke.janajah right there.

00:10:43.476 --> 00:10:45.644 line:0%
Thank you so much for coming on.

00:10:45.644 --> 00:10:48.380
Our thanks to all the creators
for joining me tonight.

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:49.982
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:49.982 --> 00:10:51.750
Thank you very much
for being here. Stick around.

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:54.319
We'll be right back
with Milo Ventimiglia, everyone.

00:10:54.319 --> 00:10:55.821
Come on back.

00:10:55.821 --> 00:10:59.491 line:0%
I can't do -- I can't do --
I can't even do that.

00:10:59.491 --> 00:11:00.592 line:0%
I'll do that.

